# Testing Electron Applications

Extends `core/rules/testing.mdc`. Examples use Vitest; renderer component testing follows the React rules.

---

## Main Process

- Keep business logic in plain services with no `electron` import; unit test them directly
- Export IPC handler functions separately from their `ipcMain.handle` registration so they can be called with a fake event
- Mock `electron` only at the boundary (`app`, `BrowserWindow`, `dialog`)

```typescript
vi.mock('electron', () => ({
  app: { on: vi.fn(), quit: vi.fn(), getPath: vi.fn(() => '/tmp') },
  BrowserWindow: vi.fn(),
  ipcMain: { handle: vi.fn() },
}));

it('rejects an untrusted sender', async () => {
  const event = { senderFrame: { url: 'https://evil.example' } } as unknown as IpcMainInvokeEvent;
  await expect(saveFileHandler(event, 'data')).rejects.toThrow('Untrusted sender');
});

it('rejects an oversized payload', async () => {
  await expect(saveFileHandler(trustedEvent, 'x'.repeat(2_000_000))).rejects.toThrow();
});
```

---

## IPC Handlers

- Test sender validation and payload validation for every handler (valid, wrong type, too large, wrong origin)
- Assert structured error results, not just "throws"
- Test that window-scoped listeners are removed when the window closes

---

## Preload and Renderer

- Renderer code talks to `window.api` only — mock it in tests (`vi.stubGlobal('api', { saveFile: vi.fn() })`)
- Do not import `electron` from renderer tests; if you need to, the renderer is coupled to Node
- Test hooks that subscribe to IPC events clean up on unmount (`renderHook` from `@testing-library/react`)

---

## End-to-End (Playwright)

- Use Playwright's Electron support (Spectron is dead); launch the **built** app
- Use an isolated `userData` directory per test run
- Cover critical flows end to end, plus security smoke checks (e.g. `window.require` and `process` are undefined in the renderer)

```typescript
import { _electron as electron, expect, test } from '@playwright/test';

test('saves a document', async () => {
  const app = await electron.launch({ args: ['out/main/index.js'], env: { ...process.env, APP_ENV: 'test' } });
  const window = await app.firstWindow();
  expect(await window.evaluate(() => typeof (window as any).require)).toBe('undefined');
  await window.getByRole('button', { name: 'Save' }).click();
  await expect(window.getByText('Saved')).toBeVisible();
  await app.close();
});
```

---

## Checklist

- [ ] Services tested without Electron; handlers tested with fake events
- [ ] Every handler has sender- and payload-validation tests
- [ ] Renderer tests mock `window.api`, never `electron`
- [ ] Playwright E2E against the built app with isolated user data
- [ ] Renderer security smoke test (no Node globals)
